/* 2026-08-08: Stop hours — split-hours listings stop leaking the raw 🏛 line. A stop can name a day once and cut it into two windows ("🏛 Daily 9:00am - 12:00pm · 3:00pm - 6:00pm"); the afternoon segment carries a time range and no day word, so _seg returned null, which set bad = true and skipped the WHOLE stop — leaving the authored 🏛 row visible to the reader, which is exactly the leak the 2026-08-08 🏛 ban names. 69 hours blocks across 46 guides, every one failing for this single reason (Aix-en-Provence, Bologna, Florence, Dublin, Abu Dhabi, Colmar, Hiroshima and 39 more). _seg now returns a bare range as { cont: true } and the merge loop attaches it to the PRECEDING segment's days, appending rather than overwriting so the day reads "9:00am – 12:00pm, 3:00pm – 6:00pm"; windows chain, so Dublin's Sunday carries three (9–10:30, 12:45–2:30, 4:30–6). Only days the anchoring segment actually wrote are extended, so a day already claimed by an earlier segment keeps its own hours — Abu Dhabi's Friday split does not bleed into its Saturday–Thursday run. Three shapes stay deliberately unreadable and still leave the stop alone: a continuation with nothing before it, one following Open 24/7 or a closed day, and a bare "Closed" with no day. The same root cause is fixed in the Open Now filter, which was answering "Closed" at 4pm on these very stops: _segOpen now reports day-coverage and open-ness separately so _hoursOpen can lend a continuation the day of the segment it continues, and it gained the single-named-day form ("Friday 9:00am - 12:00pm") it never handled — the reason every Gulf Friday listing read as unparseable. Verified by driving the real shipped parser over all 3,140 hours blocks in the fleet: 0 remaining leaks, no regressions, and 15 open-now cases (both windows, the lunch gap, after close, and the day-boundary cases) correct. Locked by check_stop_hours_contract contract 7, which runs the real _seg + merge loop under node rather than grepping for the branch — smoke-tested to FAIL on both a reverted _seg and a gutted merge loop. toolbar.js -> v226. CACHE to v356. */
